(3299392, 459893, 200, '<td valign="top">This is nice. I wish her face and fingers were not cropped out..that her neck were a little more relaxed and accepting of the moment. If i crop the left side out and no longer see the right hand and tense neck, then i no longer see a sense of discomfort and i can focus on the beauty of the body. Its really a very beautiful image when i crop out the discomfort. I hope you will try that.</td>', 'This is nice. I wish her face and fingers were not cropped out..that her neck were a little more relaxed and accepting of the moment. If i crop the left side out and no longer see the right hand and tense neck, then i no longer see a sense of discomfort and i can focus on the beauty of the body. Its really a very beautiful image when i crop out the discomfort. I hope you will try that.', '2007-01-29 15:33:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(3299401, 460253, 40679, '<td valign="top">this is a bit of a weird entry. not bad weird, but artsy. it intruiges me. the drops of light on the bodies are a pretty add, and the almost candid-feel is beautiful, allthough I don''t usually like that.<br/> <br/>your entry is getting a high vote from me.</td>', 'this is a bit of a weird entry. not bad weird, but artsy. it intruiges me. the drops of light on the bodies are a pretty add, and the almost candid-feel is beautiful, allthough I don''t usually like that. your entry is getting a high vote from me.', '2007-01-29 15:35:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(3299402, 460137, 26255, '<td valign="top">Typically with a high key infant shot, I prefer to see a softer focus.  I''m afraid you''ve pushed this one a bit too far and what appears to be wings of some sort get lost in all the brightness.  Poses like this also work better if the legs are under the baby.  I do realize this is difficult to achieve, but with a little care and patience, you can eventually get it.  Next time, try lighting the background from an angle behind the baby with a softer fill flash to light the baby.  I''ve used an off camera slave flash on white foamboard behind the baby and a softer strobe to light the baby on this exact same shot in the past.  You''ve got a good start, a little more experimentation and practice will get you a much better shot.</td>', 'Typically with a high key infant shot, I prefer to see a softer focus.  I''m afraid you''ve pushed this one a bit too far and what appears to be wings of some sort get lost in all the brightness.  Poses like this also work better if the legs are under the baby.  I do realize this is difficult to achieve, but with a little care and patience, you can eventually get it.  Next time, try lighting the background from an angle behind the baby with a softer fill flash to light the baby.  I''ve used an off camera slave flash on white foamboard behind the baby and a softer strobe to light the baby on this exact same shot in the past.  You''ve got a good start, a little more experimentation and practice will get you a much better shot.', '2007-01-29 15:36:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(3299404, 459808, 50641, '<td valign="top">too much neat image!  j/k  ....good luck!</td>', 'too much neat image!  j/k  ....good luck!', '2007-01-29 15:36:31.000000', NULL, 1),
