(3351659, 459524, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Flower Bath" is a good entry into the Nude IV challenge.  I think you did a very good job at being creative and taking a different path from the norm. <br/> <br/>Overall I think this is a very pleasing image, and I really love the flowers.  The coloring of the flowers is bright but very mellow.  Its amazing how unreal the flowers look, but the image still looks natural.  I also think her eyes have a prefect glow and draw the viewer in.  I can easily see the shot hanging in a bathroom.  The editing that you did not great, I don''t think the shot is over processed.  It was interesting on some of the comments how this shot is too sweet, really makes you wonder about the world we are living.  <br/> <br/>I can see that you have only done a couple of challenges but you look like you have a great balance of creativity and photography skills.  I really look forward to see what you produce in the future. <br/></td>', '*Critique Club* "Flower Bath" is a good entry into the Nude IV challenge.  I think you did a very good job at being creative and taking a different path from the norm.  Overall I think this is a very pleasing image, and I really love the flowers.  The coloring of the flowers is bright but very mellow.  Its amazing how unreal the flowers look, but the image still looks natural.  I also think her eyes have a prefect glow and draw the viewer in.  I can easily see the shot hanging in a bathroom.  The editing that you did not great, I don''t think the shot is over processed.  It was interesting on some of the comments how this shot is too sweet, really makes you wonder about the world we are living.   I can see that you have only done a couple of challenges but you look like you have a great balance of creativity and photography skills.  I really look forward to see what you produce in the future. ', '2007-02-10 20:41:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3351689, 459556, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"The Sad Geisha" is a very good entry into the Nude IV challenge.  I like that you were able to capture something a little more unusual. I have to give you huge credit for doing a self portrait, you are far courageous then most. <br/> <br/>The photo is very striking just based on the concept of what it is.  I think the choice to not be happy works very well for this piece.  Also I think black and white allows us to focus on the subject and not be distracted by possible bright colors.  The one thing I could see changing about the shot is the lighting.  I think because we have such a soft subject the lighting should be very soft to capture you.  I might even try the majority of the lighting to come from the left and then a soft light from the right to keep the shadows away.<br/> <br/>This really is a great piece especially for your 3rd challenge.  Nice job! <br/></td>', '*Critique Club* "The Sad Geisha" is a very good entry into the Nude IV challenge.  I like that you were able to capture something a little more unusual. I have to give you huge credit for doing a self portrait, you are far courageous then most.  The photo is very striking just based on the concept of what it is.  I think the choice to not be happy works very well for this piece.  Also I think black and white allows us to focus on the subject and not be distracted by possible bright colors.  The one thing I could see changing about the shot is the lighting.  I think because we have such a soft subject the lighting should be very soft to capture you.  I might even try the majority of the lighting to come from the left and then a soft light from the right to keep the shadows away. This really is a great piece especially for your 3rd challenge.  Nice job! ', '2007-02-10 20:54:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3351716, 460210, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Nude Beauty" is a good entry into the Nude IV challenge, l like it because it is something different.  I am really impressed how creative everyone was during this challenge.<br/> <br/>I think it is very interesting that you commented that you had taken this shot at night.  I am just wondering if maybe you stated that because you would have shot it differently during the day.  I really like the shape that has been created in this shot, the lines draw you in towards the center.  The focus looks like maybe you were focusing more on the elbows, I think even if you used a shallow depth of field and focus on the glass it might have drawn in more voters.  I like the glow that was created by the light, it feels like it is the lines are moving us into the shot.  The over framing of the subject is very good, it doesn''t feel over cropped. <br/> <br/>Nice work! <br/></td>', '*Critique Club* "Nude Beauty" is a good entry into the Nude IV challenge, l like it because it is something different.  I am really impressed how creative everyone was during this challenge. I think it is very interesting that you commented that you had taken this shot at night.  I am just wondering if maybe you stated that because you would have shot it differently during the day.  I really like the shape that has been created in this shot, the lines draw you in towards the center.  The focus looks like maybe you were focusing more on the elbows, I think even if you used a shallow depth of field and focus on the glass it might have drawn in more voters.  I like the glow that was created by the light, it feels like it is the lines are moving us into the shot.  The over framing of the subject is very good, it doesn''t feel over cropped.  Nice work! ', '2007-02-10 21:05:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3351743, 460250, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Blue Baby" is very cool concept for the Nude challenge. <br/> <br/>I think that the idea is fabulous and what a wonderful girlfriend to model for you.  I defiantly voted for you on this one for the creativity.  I think to make the photo scores some what higher you might try and have the background tight.  The subtle wrinkles and sag on the left hand side are kind of distracting.  I like the way the lighting allows a soft shadow to be cast onto the background.  The lighting is a great piece, the only thing I would say is to some take the shot without the glare off the guitar.  I think I like the tint of the image it gives you something a little different from bright colors and black and white.  I am surprised with the title you didn''t want to give the shot a small blue tint, but then it might look too cold.  Also you did a great job with the focus and composition. <br/> <br/>Overall very nice job, keep up the good work! <br/></td>', '*Critique Club* "Blue Baby" is very cool concept for the Nude challenge.  I think that the idea is fabulous and what a wonderful girlfriend to model for you.  I defiantly voted for you on this one for the creativity.  I think to make the photo scores some what higher you might try and have the background tight.  The subtle wrinkles and sag on the left hand side are kind of distracting.  I like the way the lighting allows a soft shadow to be cast onto the background.  The lighting is a great piece, the only thing I would say is to some take the shot without the glare off the guitar.  I think I like the tint of the image it gives you something a little different from bright colors and black and white.  I am surprised with the title you didn''t want to give the shot a small blue tint, but then it might look too cold.  Also you did a great job with the focus and composition.  Overall very nice job, keep up the good work! ', '2007-02-10 21:13:00.000000', NULL, 0),
